    description: "Package coverage-directed selection as a git hook -- the framing the idea\nstarted from -- so selection happens at commit time rather than only when\nsmart-test is invoked.\n\nGOVERNANCE: .githooks/** requires human approval. This must be a SEPARATE PR\nfrom any smart-test work and must not be bundled. Per AGENTS.md: set the item\nto needs_human_review, post the proposed change for approval, and only then\nrun auto-pr.\n\nDEFERRED DELIBERATELY. The machinery (block hashing, incremental index, git\nbaseline) is now in scripts/smart-test and hypergumbo_core, which are not\ngovernance files. A hook adds no capability -- it changes only WHEN selection\nruns -- so it earns nothing until the selector itself is trusted (Phase 2+)."  # f619
    fields: {}  # f619
